  "id": "COMPOUND:7929 - PROTEIN:4978",
  "verbalization": "Etofenamate is implicated in the regulation of C8166 through a series of molecular interactions involving 5-hydroxytryptamine receptors. The evidence suggests that Etofenamate acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Licoricesaponin G2, 7,10-Epoxy-Ar-Bisabol-11-Ol, and Kahiricoside II, all of which are known to interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Etofenamate may influence C8166 through the activation of this receptor. The overlapping targets suggest a possible shared pathway or functional relationship between Etofenamate and C8166, possibly through the modulation of neurotransmitter signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1 in mediating the effects of Etofenamate on C8166, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
